  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "note": "Ewe 'ga {h}' (ga = o'clock, from gaƒoƒo 'bell strike'), additive 'ga {h} kple aɖabaƒoƒo N' (aɖabaƒoƒo = minute, already used by this locale) and 'ga {h} kple afã' (half). Ewe numerals: atɔ̃, ewo, wuiatɔ̃, blaeve, blaetɔ̃, blaene, blaatɔ̃ with 'vɔ' for the units. Standard 12-hour count. No subtractive form: Ewe speakers mostly state hour + minutes."
    }
